      whyItMatters: "Technology selection is the third-most important SC decision after operating model and organizational structure — but it is often treated as the first. Buying a world-class planning tool and running a 1990s S&OP process on top of it is the most expensive mistake in FMCG SC transformation. The technology landscape briefing exists to help consultants navigate vendor conversations with clients and ground technology selection in genuine business requirements.",
      technologyEnablers: "**Demand Planning / S&OP:**\n- SAP IBP: Most common in large FMCG; strong SAP integration. Implementation complexity high.\n- o9 Solutions: Strong in FMCG; modern interface; better external signal integration. Growing in India.\n- Kinaxis RapidResponse: Best-in-class for scenario planning; stronger in complex global SC.\n- Blue Yonder: Strong in demand and fulfillment; some India FMCG deployments.\n\n**Distribution Technology (India-Specific):**\n- Beatroute: Leading Indian DMS; strong in general trade; mobile-first. Used by Marico, Godrej CP.\n- Bizom: Strong DMS + trade promotion management; data analytics differentiator.\n- Shotgun: Emerging; strong mobile UX; suited for mid-size FMCG.\n\n**WMS:**\n- SAP EWM: Enterprise grade; suited for large centralized DCs.\n- Manhattan Associates: Strong in FMCG; good for high-velocity ambient goods.\n- Infor WMS: Mid-market option; faster implementation.",
      consultingEntryPoints: "**Trigger:** Client is selecting a demand planning tool and evaluating multiple vendors.\n**Thoucentric Angle:** Technology selection advisory — requirements definition, vendor evaluation, business case\n**Engagement Type:** Advisory\n\n**Trigger:** Client has deployed a planning tool but is not realizing expected benefits.\n**Thoucentric Angle:** Value realization assessment — process gap analysis, adoption improvement, configuration optimization\n**Engagement Type:** Diagnostic + Transformation",
